---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Corrections & Clarifications Policy"
  description="newskrypt procedure for acknowledging, correcting, and documenting factual errors promptly and transparently."
  canonicalUrl="https://crypto-news-rose.vercel.app/corrections"
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 md:py-20">
    <header class="mb-10 pb-6 border-b border-slate-200">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 bg-amber-500/10 border border-amber-500/30 rounded-full text-xs font-extrabold text-amber-800 uppercase tracking-wider mb-4">
        <span>⚖️ Factual Accountability & Transparency</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-black text-black tracking-tight mb-3">
        Corrections & Factual Accountability Policy
      </h1>
      <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 font-medium">Last Reviewed & Formally Ratified: September 2026 | Editorial Integrity Desk</p>
    </header>

    <div class="space-y-8 text-sm text-black leading-relaxed">
      <!-- Section 1: Core Commitment -->
      <section class="bg-white border border-slate-200 p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-2xl shadow-xs">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-black mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>1. Journalistic Truth & Immediate Error Correction</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="text-black mb-3">
          At <strong>newskrypt</strong>, factual accuracy is the absolute foundation of our financial newsroom. We hold ourselves to the highest canons of financial journalism. When a factual error, calculation flaw, or material omission occurs in any of our published reports, market breakdowns, or regulatory articles, our policy is to correct it immediately, transparently, and publicly.
        </p>
        <p class="text-black">
          We strictly prohibit "stealth editing" - silently changing substantive factual claims without disclosing the edit to our readers.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 2: Transparent Correction Protocol -->
      <section class="bg-white border border-slate-200 p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-2xl shadow-xs">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-black mb-3">2. Step-by-Step Correction Protocol</h2>
        <p class="text-black mb-4">
          When an error is brought to our attention via internal review, reader tips, or subject feedback, the <strong>newskrypt</strong> newsroom executes a mandatory 3-step protocol:
        </p>

        <div class="space-y-4">
          <div class="p-4 bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200 rounded-xl">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-black text-base mb-1">Step 1: Rapid Verification & Primary Source Check</h3>
            <p class="text-slate-800 text-xs sm:text-sm">
              The senior editor on duty immediately checks the flagged statement against official regulatory documentation (SEC, BaFin, MiCA), on-chain transaction hashes, or verified primary court filings.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-4 bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200 rounded-xl">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-black text-base mb-1">Step 2: Immediate Article Correction & Disclosure</h3>
            <p class="text-slate-800 text-xs sm:text-sm">
              The inaccuracy is corrected in the live text. An explicit, highlighted <strong>"Correction Notice"</strong> block is appended to the article stating clearly: (a) what was incorrect, (b) what the accurate facts are, and (c) the date and exact timestamp of the correction.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-4 bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200 rounded-xl">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-black text-base mb-1">Step 3: Syndication & Social Footprint Update</h3>
            <p class="text-slate-800 text-xs sm:text-sm">
              If the erroneous detail was distributed via RSS feeds, official email dispatches, or social channels, a formal clarification post or updated feed entry is issued to ensure readers across all platforms receive the correct information.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 3: Alignment with Editorial & Publishing Standards -->
      <section class="bg-white border border-slate-200 p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-2xl shadow-xs">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-black mb-3">3. Integration with Core Editorial & Publishing Rules</h2>
        <p class="text-black mb-3">
          Our corrections policy operates in tandem with all mandatory publishing rules governing <strong>newskrypt</strong>:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-black">
          <li><strong>Image Integrity:</strong> Articles maintain non-duplicate, unique hero images with exact descriptive alt text matching the subject matter. If an image caption or infographic is inaccurate, it is updated and noted in accordance with our <a href="/editorial-policy" class="text-amber-600 font-bold hover:underline">Editorial Policy</a>.</li>
          <li><strong>Heading & SEO Calibration:</strong> Article titles and metaTitles adhere strictly to our 55-character length target and unique keyword rules, preventing misleading or clickbait headlines.</li>
          <li><strong>YMYL Financial Non-Advisory Guarantee:</strong> Corrections to financial data (such as yield figures or liquidation volumes) are handled with extreme urgency to prevent reader misinterpretation under Google's YMYL quality guidelines.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 4: How to Report an Inaccuracy -->
      <section class="bg-white border border-slate-200 p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-2xl shadow-xs">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-black mb-3">4. How to Submit a Correction Request</h2>
        <p class="text-black mb-3">
          We welcome vigilance from our readers, researchers, and community members. If you spot a factual error, please email our Standards & Integrity Desk with the following information:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 text-black">
          <li><strong>Article URL:</strong> The full canonical link of the story on <code class="bg-white px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-black border border-slate-300">crypto-news-rose.vercel.app</code>.</li>
          <li><strong>Specific Inaccuracy:</strong> The exact quote, figure, or sentence in question.</li>
          <li><strong>Primary Documentation:</strong> Verifiable primary sources (on-chain transaction link, regulatory filing PDF, or official press release).</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="mt-6 p-4 bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200 rounded-xl">
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-800">
            Send your correction request directly to our Senior Standards Editor at:
            <code class="block mt-2 font-mono text-xs font-bold text-amber-700">newskryptowahrung26@gmail.com</code>
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>